It is Thursday evening, half past five.
I am at the badminton club and go to the reception first.
"Hello, I need a racket again, please," I say.
The employee gives me the racket and wishes me a lot of fun.
Then I walk into the big hall.
Summer is here and it is extremely hot in here.
Lena and Timo are already waving at me.
Today I am playing with a new partner against the two of them.
Our doubles match is tough and we sweat a lot.
The shuttlecock flies quickly back and forth over the net.
After the game, we are all completely exhausted.
We sit down together on the benches by the wall.
I catch my breath and drink some water.
"That was a very fast game," Lena laughs.
"Yes, your rallies were really great," I answer.
We sit there for a while longer and chat about the game.
Slowly we cool down.
I am tired, but the training feels good.
